# Laravel docs + beginner code

## Main reference

Use https://laravel.com/framework/docs/ as the primary guide for structure and Artisan commands (routing, middleware, migrations, Eloquent, Blade, CSRF, validation, auth).

Class progress for Lab Act 2 starts from Migrations: https://laravel.com/framework/docs/migrations

## Laravel version truth

This app is **Laravel 11** (`petal-express/composer.json`). Prefer docs concepts. Do not copy Laravel 13-only APIs. If an example disagrees with this codebase, follow Laravel 11 + existing `petal-express` patterns.

## Beginner style (required)

- Thin controllers, plain comments, short methods
- Blade + Breeze only. No React in this lab app
- Prefer `php artisan make:*` from the docs
- No Spatie Permission or other role packages. Use a simple `users.role` column + middleware
- Eloquent for the graded CRUD path (`Post::all()`, `Post::create([...])`). Query Builder only as oral-defense comparison, not the main path
- Keep Petal Express theme (cream page, accent `#4f6fa5`, brand `petal express`)

## Database for Lab Act 2

SQLite only: `DB_CONNECTION=sqlite` and `petal-express/database/database.sqlite`. Do not switch to PostgreSQL or Supabase unless the human explicitly asks after a PDF requires it.

## Lab Act 1 patterns to match

- Routes in `petal-express/routes/web.php` with named routes
- Guest pages via controllers + Blade; member pages behind `auth`
- Forms use `@csrf`; contact-style static forms flash thank-you without DB insert when the brief says static

